{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/241110-testing-game-advice-needed","id":241110,"title":"Testing game, advice needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-25T23:00:27-07:00","id":241110,"title":"Testing game, advice needed","content":"Crossposting this from rpg.net...<br /> <br /> So my girlfriend and I are both avid GMs with an interest in running <i>Demon: The Descent.</i> More particularly, she wants to run it and I really want to play it. Demons got a lot of cool little parts to it that we're a bit nervous about dragging our group into without knowing how things will work in practice. In that spirit, we've decided that I'll run a short thing where she's playing an individual Demon and try to explore some of Demons mechanics while doing this. I'm looking for some advice on how to put meat on the backbone of a story I've got in my head so far.<br /> <br /> So the character she has is a Psychopomp Saboteur whose job used to be to deliver objects for the God-Machine to various sites, with a Cover as a little girl delivering newspapers. This Psychopomp fell when they realized that they wanted freedom of movement beyond the confines of what the God-Machine directed it to do, and it decided the only way for it to be totally free is to fight back against the Machine by becoming a Saboteur.<br /> <br /> So we've got a character sheet and all. The only real details that are external are that they have a dot of Contacts which is &quot;Saboteurs&quot; which I'm taking to think they communicate with the local Soldiers. They also have a single dot of Mentor, which she wants to be a member of the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Shade, the Psychopomp, doesn't identify with its Cover in any personal way, and sees it as a means to an end to remain hidden from the God-Machine. Shade's Virtue is Hidden, which echoes the strong emphasis on stealthy delivery that we've concepted for it pre-Fall, while its vice is Curious. It was curious about why it was confined to specific routes, about what it was carrying, about what else it could do. I definitely think the conflict between that Virtue/Vice combo will be fairly defining for Shade.<br /> <br /> So that's most of the character details. I'm setting our little playtest in Seattle, and I have the latest Demon releases from having backed the Kickstarter. One of the things I noticed in <i>Flowers of Hell</i> was the excellent section on Infrastructure. It gives a lot of details on Infrastructure and how to interact with it. I think the thing that stuck out to me the most were the examples. While I was reading through it earlier today, I noticed one that I decided would be the basis for what I wanted to run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flowers of Hell, pg. 70</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ubiquitous white vans have been parked all around the neighborhood for weeks, uniformed men opening the road-side cabinets containing telephone wires and installing new hardware. The residents all received notice of cable works in the mail, promises of super fast downloads and uninterrupted television, but the cables the workers are installing aren't fiber-optic. They're black, rubbery, and have a <i>pulse.</i> At the center of the tangled web of streets laid with new Infrastructure, the Linchpin resides in the local exchange - beneath the gray panels of the hardware, the cables knot together into a black, pulsating mass. Demons interfering with the Infrastructure can gain a way into hundreds of homes, influencing the people living inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, definitely want to use that one. I'm thinking the computers and televisions hooked up to these wires do bring their promised faster speeds and uninterrupted television, but that they also bring subliminal messages to people. I'm thinking those messages might help to popularize a nearby park that just underwent some renovation a year ago, passively encouraging the people in the neighborhood to visit the park and spend time there...<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking, how will my player's Demon stumble upon this? When they're living in their Cover I decided, they'd be delivering papers in the neighborhood and maybe they noticed the letters. Maybe it was the vans. This is where I'm not sure. Would a Demon be able to sense the Infrastructure at work? How would I render this in narrative? I have the idea that the letters all smell faintly like ionized air to the Demon (in reality, its their senses interpreting a faint residue of Aether, which they'd know) but I'm not sure if it should be the letters or the vans or what.<br /> <br /> So, given the character's Saboteur nature, I honestly expect that they'll want to destroy the linchpin and stop this infrastructure. Seems simple enough, I'm just wondering: What should be the catch? The twist, if any? First, I'm definitely thinking there's some kind of minor Guardian angel who is overseeing the linchpin itself. I'm tempted to make whatever the cable company is in the city into some sort of obfuscated subsidiary of the Deva Corporation. Maybe the people providing security are part of Deva's security shell company? So they're overseen by an Angel. Could be plenty tough, even if there's only a couple or trio of them. That brings <i>some complications</i> into it on the side of the opposition. Cool!<br /> <br /> Of course, I feel like I shouldn't just involve Shade all by itself. Maybe there's another Demon too, with an agenda which would conflict with Shade's? Maybe this other Demon just doesn't trust Shade to not be reliable or wants the infrastructure to help create a cult or something. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> Any suggestions on additional details or ideas are really appreciated! I want to explore as many of Demon's key concepts as I reasonably can within the confines of this story. If there's anything here you think is a problem or silly or not exploring an idea to its full potential, hearing about that would be excellent as well!<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading/helping!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T02:38:17-07:00","id":241189,"title":"","content":"You can explore the contact &quot;Saboteurs&quot;. They could be an Agency in need of some help with this strange neighborhood. They tell her there was an Inquisitor seeking the truth and he got missing. His ring broke into his apartment and they found this *they show her a photo of a little girl with a newspaper on hand, only that her hair color is different*. I would want to make it personal, so while she investigates she would see that girl from the photo, God-machine found a substitute, another angel who is taking over her old position. <br /> <br /> And she is bringing an update to this infrastructure, God-machine wants to try something more risky after the initial sucess. Something bold. And if by tv or internet God-machine could reprogram the human mind and create semi-stigmatics capable of reporting any suspicious activities such as demons? If it works this can change the city forever, as they woukd have to deal with hundreds of ordinary people spying on them. If it fails, this mortal minds will stay lost forever, forcing God-machine to eliminate them all. Anyway, he is protecting his new project with three stigmatic cops and one angel - $37\u00a57362N, the lady in red, cover: street prostitute. Nicknames: the Queen of the Darkest Night, The Lady who dress with Blood. Ban: cannot move more than 3 streets away from the linchpin Bane: copper<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this can give you a few ideas how to run Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T14:08:54-07:00","id":241704,"title":"","content":"We elected to drop the Mentor merit in favor of another Contact, reflecting the Cover's connections with people in the neighborhood.<br /> <br /> The Saboteurs contact was changed to a particular Tempter who goes by the alias Big Top. He has a fondness for street performer covers, which he uses to spy on people in parks and other places, looking for people that want/need pacts. Shade helped save him from a Hunter that figured him for some kind of Demon clown once, and as a compensation, he told her his performing route, that way she can find him easily to ask him questions.<br /> <br /> I don't want to necessarily go overboard with this plot, since it's supposed to be a bit of a playtest. A thought I had is that the park which they might be subliminally encouraged to go to would have a concert, at which a tragedy might occur. Said tragedy might provide the fuel to summon an Angel for another piece of infrastructure.<br /> <br /> As for the Guardian that's watching over the Infrastructure, I'm thinking it's probably a Rank 2 Angel, and I'm tempted to have its Influence and powers centered around the electrical wiring in the local exchange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 08-29-2014, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T21:26:53-07:00","id":247436,"title":"","content":"Made an angel to guard the Logistics Infrastructure, let me know what you think:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Wire Spider</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mission: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wire Spider was created to defend the Logistical Infrastructure being set up in Virtual Citadel\u2019s Data Center in Downtown Seattle. It has some security guards to assist in its mission, but it is by far the most potent of the Data Center\u2019s defenders. While Wire Spider is not the most powerful of Angels, its patience and economical use of its abilities can serve to draw in its targets to take care of them discretely, as it has done with a few employees that got too nosey. Their bodies will never be found in the sea of wires beneath the Data Center.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Description:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Wire Spider\u2019s entire body is composed of the wires that are its namesake, mixing and weaving into a thick body of red, green and yellow wires, with white wires decorating it\u2019s \u201cthorax\u201d in complex circuitry. Its four pairs of eyes are made of wall mounted warning lights, which alight faintly as they catch the light. It\u2019s often hard to distinguish Wire Spider from the web of cables and wires which coat the floors and walls of its lair.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Methods:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Wire Spider prefers to allow its prey to come to it. It might taunt them with some of its Numen and Manifestations to drag them down beneath the Data Center, isolating them from anyone that might call for help. Then it strikes. It usually drags its targets to the floor to attack them with its fangs that vaguely resemble wire caps. It hides in and around the wiring in its lair to attempt sneak attacks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Virtue: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Patient</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Vice: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sadistic</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rank: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Attributes: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Influence: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Wires 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Corpus: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Willpower:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> 9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Size: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Speed: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">15</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Defense: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Initiative: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Armor: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1/0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weapon/Attack:</span></b></span></span><ul><li><b>Wire Cap Fangs:</b> +1L Melee, <b>Dice Pool:</b> 10 - Defense</li> <li><b>Electrified Wires:</b> +0L 50/100/200, <b>Dice Pool:</b> 10, <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Numina:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Trip (As Embed; wires trip enemy), Blast (electrified wires), Innocous, Implant Mission, Signs (Text messages, wall markers, emails and screens)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Manifestations:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Twilight Form, Materialize, Image, Possess</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Max Essence: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">20</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ban: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wire Spider must immediately dematerialize if the power to the building is shut off.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bane: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wire Cutters.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T23:05:43-07:00","id":253042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/241110-testing-game-advice-needed#post241110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossposting this from rpg.net...<br /> <br /> Yeah, definitely want to use that one. I'm thinking the computers and televisions hooked up to these wires do bring their promised faster speeds and uninterrupted television, but that they also bring subliminal messages to people. I'm thinking those messages might help to popularize a nearby park that just underwent some renovation a year ago, passively encouraging the people in the neighborhood to visit the park and spend time there...</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons have the ability to detect infrastructure, both by sight and by aetheric resonance whenever they process essence. The G-M can counteract this to some extent by using concealment infrastructure.<br /> <br /> For Shade's interaction with his ring-mates, hmmm.... Given that his Vice is Curious, I'm surprised he's no an Inquisitor. What's his personal stake in seeing the G-M? Expand on his catalyst. What made him want to take<br /> <br /> With his virtue of Hidden, Shade strikes me as someone with the Navy Seal mentality: if your chance of success is %100, go for it, if it's not prepare and and train until it is. If you decide that's true, who have someone who's bringing a feeling of confidence to the fight against the G-M. Remember that Hidden also applies to his own Ring mates during interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}